WEBVTT

preparation-01
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.050
Begin by washing and drying your hands.

preparation-02
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:15.150
Set the Arclight to its brightest light, push both lens racks fully up, and use a quiet, dim room.

preparation-03
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:31.500
Hold the Arclight close to your own eye, with the light just below your line of sight. This lets you look directly along the beam.

preparation-04
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:48.000
A newborn should be securely swaddled. Ask a parent to hold an older baby, while a child who can sit steadily may sit on their own.

examination-01
00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.950
Start at about arm's length.

examination-02
00:00:53.300 --> 00:01:03.850
Move gently from side to side, and come a little closer only if you need a clearer view.

examination-03
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:19.850
At about arm's length, keep both eyes in view together.

examination-04
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:31.900
There should be no difference in the brightness or colour of the two fundal reflexes.

examination-05
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:46.650
Normal reflex colour varies with retinal pigmentation. It may appear yellow-white or bluish, orange-red, or orange-yellow.

eyes-open-01
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:57.600
Ask the parent to hold the newborn securely, swaddled with the arms tucked in.

eyes-open-02
00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:04.950
With the eyes open, observe both reflexes together without touching the baby.

eyes-open-03
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:13.600
Do not touch the baby's face or eyelids to obtain the view.

eyes-closed-01
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:21.200
If the baby is asleep, there is no need to wake them.

eyes-closed-02
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:35.150
Gently open and examine one eye at a time.

possible-findings-01
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:47.700
Brief, occasional squints are common in the first month and usually disappear by three months.

unclear-findings-01
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:56.600
If the finding is unclear, follow these three steps.

unclear-findings-02
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:06.600
First, compare the baby's reflex with the parent's. They should look similar.

unclear-findings-03
00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:13.600
If you are still unsure, ask a colleague for a second opinion.

unclear-findings-04
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:23.300
If no colleague is available, obtain consent to make a short video.

unclear-findings-05
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:36.650
Attach the Arclight to the phone camera, record the reflex, and share the video securely for a second opinion.

possible-findings-02
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:44.600
Similar colour and brightness in both eyes are reassuring.

possible-findings-03
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:54.400
A colour difference, or partial or complete loss of a reflex, is abnormal and needs further assessment.

after-examination-01
00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:59.450
Thank the parent and explain the findings and next steps.

after-examination-02
00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:04.550
Finally, wash and dry your hands again.
